n lint:check` 0 errors, 1\npre-existing warning (AdminPanel useAiPlugin.js).\nPinned: async=true and async \"true\" answer at once (end=false, task queued, no select, no sleep); DEFAULT_SHARD_KEY\nwithout `shardkey` query forces sync, with it stays async; sync loop sleeps CONVERT_ASYNC_DELAY=1000 ms per poll and\nreturns `<base>/conv_<key>_<format>/output.pdf`, filetype pdf; with timeout 3000 ms, CONVERT_TIMEOUT after exactly 4\nsleeps (strict `>`); Err -> status_info; ErrToReload -> status_info + cleanupErrToReload; NeedParams -> UNKNOWN; no row\n-> UNKNOWN; stale last_open_date -> CONVERT_TIMEOUT even if Ok; existing Ok task not re-queued and no sleep; status\nNone re-queued; bad outputtype -> CONVERT_PARAMS before any upsert; auth code passed through; exception -> UNKNOWN;\nconvertXml -> isJson=false.\nDecisions: jest.mock factories for taskresult (requireActual spread), DocsCoServer, canvasservice, wopiClient,\nstorage-base; utils (fillResponse, sleep, getConvertionTimeout, getBaseUrlByRequest) and Context.prototype\n(initFromRequest, initTenantCache) stubbed with jest.spyOn, because utils/operationContext require each other.\naddTask mock returns an empty iterator (consumed with `yield*`). No fake timers: sleep resolves at once.\nSurprise: earlier attempts' work was lost because it was never committed before the block; commit early.\n'''\ns=s.replace('\\n## Spawned packets', log+'\\n## Spawned packets',1)\ns=s.replace('## Lessons for the Atlas\\n','## Lessons for the Atlas\\n- converterservice: the sync wait is a 1000 ms poll of taskResult.select, so sync latency is quantized to whole seconds; CONVERT_TIMEOUT fires when waitTime > getConvertionTimeout (strict), and also whenever last_open_date is older than that timeout.\\n- To unit-test DocService modules, stub utils with jest.spyOn rather than jest.mock (utils <-> operationContext cycle).\\n',1)\nopen(f,'w').write(s)\nPY\necho '{\"packet\":\"PKT-0027\",\"role\":\"executor\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"date\":\"2026-11-02\",\"hindered\":{\"ref\":\"work-packet#protocol\",\"text\":\"Work from blocked attempts was not committed, so it was lost on release and had to be rewritten.\"},\"helped\":{\"ref\":\"work-packet#R3\",\"text\":\"Spawning the lint follow-ups instead of widening scope got the main-branch lint fixed; acceptance then passed without touching anything outside tests/unit.\"}}' >> .theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl\ngit add tests/unit/converterService.tests.js .theseus && git commit -qm \"test(docservice): characterize ConvertService sync and async flow\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git log --oneline -1 && theseus validate 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Write log, friction, commit, validate"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0027 is done and committed (`c08df45`). Both acceptance commands pass: `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` gives 150 passed and 1 skipped, and `npm run lint:check` gives 0 errors and 1 warning that was already there in AdminPanel. `theseus validate` reports no errors.\n\n**What I did:** the test file from earlier attempts was not in the worktree because it was never committed, so I wrote `tests/unit/converterService.tests.js` again. It has 17 tests that run `convertJson` and `convertXml` with the task-result store, the queue (`DocsCoServer`), `canvasservice`, `wopiClient` and storage mocked. They pin down:\n- **Async mode:** `async=true` and the string `\"true\"` answer at once with `end=false`. The task is queued, and the status is never polled and there is no wait.\n- **Shard key:** if `DEFAULT_SHARD_KEY` is set and the request has no `shardkey` query parameter, the request is forced to sync.\n- **Sync polling:** the loop waits 1000 ms per poll until the task is `Ok`, then returns the signed `output.pdf` URL. With a 3000 ms timeout, it returns `CONVERT_TIMEOUT` after exactly 4 waits, because the comparison is a strict `>`.\n- **Error statuses:**\n  - `Err` returns the row's `status_info`. `ErrToReload` returns it too and also runs a cleanup.\n  - `NeedParams` or a missing row gives `UNKNOWN`.\n  - A row whose `last_open_date` is older than the timeout gives `CONVERT_TIMEOUT`, even when its status is `Ok`.\n- **Existing tasks:** a finished (`Ok`) task is not queued again. A task with status `None` is queued again.\n- **Request errors:**\n  - A bad `outputtype` gives `CONVERT_PARAMS` before anything is written.\n  - An auth failure code is passed straight back.\n  - An exception gives `UNKNOWN`.\n- **XML:** `convertXml` follows the same flow with `isJson=false`.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- `utils` and the operation context are stubbed with `jest.spyOn`, not `jest.mock`, because the two modules require each other.\n- The `addTask` mock returns an empty iterator, because the code calls it with `yield*`.\n- No fake timers are used: `sleep` resolves at once and the timeout is set to 3000 ms.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (also written in the packet):\n- A sync conversion checks the task status once per second, so sync response times come in whole seconds.\n- `CONVERT_TIMEOUT` has two triggers: the wait time going over the timeout, and an old `last_open_date`.\n- Earlier attempts lost their work because it was never committed before the packet was blocked. Committing early would have prevented that, and I added this to the friction log.\n\nNo permissions were refused this run, and I did not request any follow-up packets.","ttft_ms":1958,"type":"result","d